        "abstract": "Outdoor location systems, such as GPS and LORAN, have been tremendously successful in the wide-area. Recently, a range of systems have been developed to extend positioning capabilities within buildings. In this talk, I’ll outline one such system, based on ultrawideband (UWB) radio, and describe both the difficulties associated with accurate in-building location and some of the applications enabled by the technology.",
        "keywords": {
            "Index Terms": [
